# `ApplicationPluginRegistrar`

<SymbolMeta />

`ApplicationPluginRegistrar` collects early, application-owned composition directives. Its declarations are resolved before dynamic builder configuration and retain `ApplicationDeclaration` provenance for diagnostics and inspection.

<SymbolSignature />

## Operations

`register` constructs a `Default` plugin; `with_plugin` retains a supplied instance. `replace` and `replace_with` select a replacement for a protocol's replaceable default slot. `suppress` explicitly disables an optional default slot. The selected plugin still has to satisfy its static relations, and a replacement cannot mutate a mandatory installation.

Use this registrar from a generated application host declaration when a plugin must be visible to generated CLI setup or participate in early composition. Do not use it as an ad hoc runtime service locator. Runtime-selected instances belong on the direct builder and are monotonic late additions.

Follow [Install through the correct boundary](/docs/latest/framework/extensions/plugins#install-through-the-correct-boundary) for the host-versus-builder workflow. The protocol counterpart is [`ProtocolPluginRegistrar`](/docs/latest/symbols/upwell_app/ProtocolPluginRegistrar).

<SymbolMembers />
